old>C</bold>).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-213-g001"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Results of sigmoidoscopic observation and histopathology in food protein-induced proctocolitis compared with the previous observations of Odze et al. and Machida et al.<sup>*</sup></p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-213-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>Odze et al. (Reference <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B9">9</xref>, <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B13">13</xref>) and Machida et al. (Reference <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B10">10</xref>). <sup>&#x02020;</sup> <italic>p</italic>=0.0001 vs. Odze's and <italic>p</italic>=0.0001 vs. Machida's. <sup>&#x02021;</sup>The maximum number of eosinophils per high-power field (HPF) (&#x000d7;400) in the single most involved biopsy was recorded. <sup>&#x000a7;</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.001 vs. Odze's and <italic>p</italic>=0.0001 vs. Machida's. <sup>&#x02225;</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.0001 vs. Machida's. EOS, eosinophil; LP, lamina propria; n.d., no data; MM, muscularis mucosa.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>